From 23d0f5f3141806558522f8d4655061ba80d14873 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 04:24:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Rendering] feat: add decals

Add a DecalComponent that projects any material onto the opaque geometry
inside a box volume, along the forward axis of its entity, to add details
such as bullet holes, signs, stains or footprints.

- RenderDecal is a RenderMesh rendered by the MeshRenderFeature, so decals
  are lit and shadowed by the existing forward and clustered lighting.
- DecalProjection.sdsl reconstructs the receiving surface (position, normal
  and tangent frame) from the depth buffer and replaces the surface streams
  before the material and the lighting are evaluated. Angle and depth fades,
  opacity, late discard to keep texture derivatives valid on the borders.
- DecalRenderFeature selects the decal shader permutation, uploads the
  per-decal parameters and sets up the volume pipeline state (back faces,
  GreaterEqual depth test, no depth write, material blend state).
- ForwardRenderer.DecalRenderStage is drawn between the opaque and the
  transparent stages with the depth buffer bound as a shader resource.
  DecalSortMode sorts decals by sort order, then creation order.
- The default graphics compositor and its template get the decal stage.
  Older graphics compositors get the DecalRenderFeature at runtime and
  render decals in the transparent stage.
- RenderSystem routes render objects to the render feature of their closest
  base type when no feature supports their exact type.
- Editor gizmo showing the projection volume and direction.
- First-person shooter template: bullet hole decals.
- Unit tests, shader compilation tests and GPU rendering tests.

Closes #24
